usf-arch-pillars : List UsfPillar
usf-arch-pillars =
  cons (usf-pillar "Cubical equality and univalence"
    "Paths are functions out of a De Morgan interval normalized in disjunctive normal form. Glue types give Voevodsky's univalence computational content (evaluating &pi;<sub>4</sub>(S<sup>3</sup>) = &minus;2), and every map factors through its observation fibers while composing equivalence witnesses along rewrites."
    "fiberEquiv f : A &simeq; (y : B) &times; ((x : A) &times; (f x &equiv; y))")
  (cons (usf-pillar "Principal-port interaction nets"
    "Definitions elaborate to Lafont interaction nets whose active pairs form exclusively between principal ports. Because redexes cannot overlap, independent cuts commute without locks or global sequence numbers, shared subgraphs duplicate lazily in O(1), and guarded corecursion runs in bounded frontier memory."
    "(u, p0) &bowtie; (v, p0) &rarr; strong confluence without global ordering")
  (cons (usf-pillar "Content-addressed store and self-hosting"
    "Every declaration, proof, and compiled module is addressed by SHA-256 digest in <code>store/&lt;sha256&gt;</code> rather than mutable filesystem paths, with zero postulates across 807 checked modules. The formalized De Bruijn evaluator and bidirectional type checker reach exact Stage-1 / Stage-2 parity."
    "store/&lt;sha256&gt; &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; sh-stage1 &equiv; sh-stage2")
  (cons (usf-pillar "Port-addressed transport and flat memory"
    "Replacing byte-stream sockets and directory hierarchies with 64-byte port-addressed frames (packing a 2<sup>6</sup>-bit 6-LUT word, moving-bit mask, and local potential) removes head-of-line blocking under packet loss, reduces content-addressed lookup to 1.12 ns in a flat mmap table, and shares pages directly between CPU and unified GPU memory."
    "((q+d)^2&minus;q^2)^2 + (2(q+d)q)^2 &equiv; ((q+d)^2+q^2)^2 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; d&omega; &equiv; 0")
  (cons (usf-pillar "Exact algebra over rings and rational geometry"
    "Multivariate polynomial normalization over Z[x<sub>1</sub>,&hellip;,x<sub>n</sub>] and sum-of-squares positivity certificates replace floating-point approximation across relativistic Dirac Hamiltonians (Z &le; 137), two-electron reduced density matrices, rational Cayley SU(2)/SE(3) kinematics, and closed-loop control barrier proofs."
    "PolyZ normal form &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; 2-RDM SOS &ge; E_0 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; det J &equiv; 1")
  (cons (usf-pillar "Mechanical lowering to hardware"
    "Typed intermediate representations lower verified programs without hand-written glue to ISO C11, WebAssembly 1.0, Apple Metal, Hopper SM_90a PTX, SystemVerilog RTL, and Sky130A / 220 nm SOI GDSII photomasks. Public nodes execute conjugated continuations whose interior boundaries cancel."
    "(E_K &circ; F &circ; D_K)^n (E_K x) &equiv; E_K (F^n x)") nil)))))
